// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/analog/mos_psp103_data.t27 -- the IHP SG13G2 PSP103 current tables, per corner, from ngspice: data and nothing else
; M3b of the analog emulation epic (#10486, issue #10516); M3c (#10777, sub-issue #10880) adds the charge tables, THE CHARGE TABLES below. M3a (specs/analog/mos_table.t27) reads a 25 x 25 table by exact-integer
; bilinear interpolation; this file holds the tables it reads when the device is the foundry's, Id(Vgs, Vds) of sg13_lv_nmos
; (W 1.0 um, L 0.45 um) and sg13_lv_pmos (W 3.0 um, L 0.45 um) for the five corners mos_tt, mos_ff, mos_ss, mos_fs and mos_sf, and the
; numbers the tests judge them by (held-out currents, the inverter's DC transfer, the inverter's transient). The functions are in
; mos_table.t27, the checks in mos_psp103.t27. Everything hand-written is the wrapper around the numbers, the pins and the accessors.
; -
; WHERE THE NUMBERS COME FROM. ngspice-47 and the IHP-Open-PDK checkout at commit 21133f219b1a6da10d803e345761e77415ceff40: the model
; file ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOSlv.lib (PSP 103.6, revision 200310) with the model code
; ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/verilog-a/psp103/psp103.va of the same commit, compiled by OpenVAF-Reloaded v24.0.2mob to psp103.osdi. Temperature
; 27 C (TNOM 27 C). The decks are plain netlists with a .control block that prints the numbers, in specs/analog/decks/:
;   psp103_tab_tt.cir, _ff, _ss, _fs, _sf   the two tables, the inverter's DC transfer, the held-out currents (the tt deck also prints the
;                                         576 cell midpoints and 1000 R2 points; the others 200 R2 points)
;   psp103_inv_be.cir, psp103_inv_fine.cir   the inverter transient at 10 pF, backward Euler on a fixed 2 ns grid and a converged run
;   psp103_inv_be_500f.cir, psp103_inv_fine_500f.cir   the same at 500 fF and 100 ps: two crossing times each (the backward Euler deck
;                                         also prints the 401-sample waveform, INV500_BE)
;   psp103_q_tt.cir, psp103_q_ss.cir   (M3c) the drain and gate charge tables, the current tables again, and the capacitances ngspice reports at one point
; Each is run as `IHP_PDK=<checkout> IHP_OSDI=<dir with psp103.osdi> ngspice -b <deck>`; no deck holds a path. ngspice rounds each current
; to a table unit itself (nint in the deck) and prints it between "BEGIN name" and "END name"; the rows were wrapped onto lines
; below in print order, none changed or reordered. The pins (order-sensitive folds, as M3a pins its run) fail on any changed number.
; -
; THE GRID AND THE UNITS. Id is tabulated on 25 x 25 nodes, 24 cells of 62.5 mV on each axis over 0 .. 1.5 V (the supply), index
; ix * 25 + iy with ix along Vgs and iy along Vds. This is the grid of M3a's reader: 24 cells of 2^20 units, so a unit is 2^-24 V
; (59.6 nV) and Vdd = 25165824. A table entry is Id * (dt / C) in volts per step, in units: dt / C = 200 V/A (2 ns on 10 pF, or 100 ps
; on 500 fF), so an entry is Id * 200 * 2^24 rounded and one unit is 0.298 nA. For the PMOS the axes are Vsg and Vsd, the source and
; bulk on the 1.5 V rail, and the entry is the current that leaves the drain. The largest entries (1.5 V, 1.5 V) are 402.3 uA (NMOS,
; 1349912) and 301.5 uA (PMOS, 1011527) at tt, below the 2^23 the solver's u64 interpolation allows. Negative entries (the gate current
; that leaves through the drain at Vds = 0 and Vgs above 1.2 V, at most 2 units = 0.6 nA) are held at 0: the table is unsigned.
; -
; THE HELD-OUT POINTS are never nodes of the grid. The tt deck prints the current in pA (nint(Id * 1e12)) at the 576 cell midpoints
; Vgs, Vds = (i + 1/2) * 62.5 mV, where a chord is worst, and at 1000 points of the R2 low-discrepancy sequence: point k = 1..1000 is
; Vgs (Vsg) = 1.5 frac(k * 0.7548776662466927) and Vds (Vsd) = 1.5 frac(k * 0.5698402909980532), 1/plastic number and its square; the
; other corners print the first 200 of those points. Each pair of devices has its own set of currents, the same coordinates.
; -
; THE CHARGE TABLES (M3c, issue #10777). Two more decks, specs/analog/decks/psp103_q_tt.cir and psp103_q_ss.cir (corners mos_tt and
; mos_ss), print the DRAIN and GATE charge of each device on the same 25 x 25 grid: TT_QD_N TT_QG_N TT_QD_P TT_QG_P and the SS_ four.
; PSP103 reports no terminal charge as an output variable (`show` lists currents, conductances and the capacitances cdd, cdg, cgg, ...
; with the overlap cgdol and junction cjd apart), so the deck takes the whole charge of a terminal, channel plus overlap plus fringe plus
; junction, from the terminal CURRENT of one backward Euler step, which is the quantity ngspice integrates: Q(B) - Q(A) = (i_A - i_return) dt
; for a step to the grid node B and back to the origin A = (Vgs, Vds) = (0, 0), dt = 10 ns, where the device is off. The same deck run
; prints the current tables (grid_n, grid_p), which are byte for byte TT_N, TT_P, SS_N, SS_P: the current tables and the charge tables come
; from one run of one netlist. A charge entry is Q / 500 fF in units of 2^-24 V (the voltage a 500 fF node moves when it takes the
; charge; one unit is 2.98e-20 C), relative to the origin plus 2^21 so that no entry is negative (only differences are physical); the PMOS
; tables are NEGATED, so that every drain table grows with Vds and every gate table with Vgs, as capacitances are positive. The scale
; ties a charge table to C = 500 fF, as a current table is tied to dt / C: for another load the entries scale by 500 fF / C.
; The tt and ss charge tables differ by 4.3 .. 5.3 % of their range, which is why the negative control in mos_psp103.t27 is the delay and
; not a count of volts.
; -
; WHAT A PASS SAYS. The numbers in this file are the numbers the decks printed, in order (the pins), the five corners are in the order
; the foundry names them (ff above tt above ss in drive current for both devices; fs a fast NMOS with a slow PMOS, sf the reverse), and
; the units are the ones the header states.
; WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. That these are the tables a board loads: the board gets the same words, but no bitstream, BRAM or UART line is
; in this milestone. That the numbers are right: they are ngspice's, at its solver tolerances (reltol 1e-6, vntol 1e-9, abstol 1e-14),
; for the two device sizes and 27 C, nothing about another W, L, m, temperature, the high-voltage devices, mismatch or Monte Carlo.
; That PSP103 is a physical transistor: it is the foundry's model of one. The drain and gate charge is tabulated for the corners tt and ss only
; (ff, fs, sf have none), the source and bulk charge not at all (a source or bulk off the rail is not a circuit this file serves), and
; a charge table is for C = 500 fF.
; ASCII only, English only.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module AnalogMosPsp103Data;

use analog::linear::{fold};

; --- what the numbers are -------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const KIND : str = "analog-table-data";
pub const ID : str = "analog/mos_psp103_data";
pub const REFERENCE : str = "IHP-Open-PDK ihp-sg13g2 cornerMOSlv.lib (PSP 103.6) through ngspice-47 and OSDI";
/// The IHP-Open-PDK checkout every number was made from.
pub const PDK_COMMIT : str = "21133f219b1a6da10d803e345761e77415ceff40";
pub const TEMP_C : u32 = 27;
/// sg13_lv_nmos: W = 1.0 um, L = 0.45 um, ng = 1, m = 1. sg13_lv_pmos: W = 3.0 um, L = 0.45 um, ng = 1, m = 1.
pub const NMOS_W_NM : u32 = 1000;
pub const PMOS_W_NM : u32 = 3000;
pub const L_NM : u32 = 450;
/// The grid: 24 cells of 62.5 mV (62500 uV) over 0 .. 1.5 V on each axis, 25 x 25 nodes.
pub const CELL_UV : u32 = 62500;
pub const VDD_MV : u32 = 1500;
/// Table entry = Id [A] * DTC_V_PER_A * UNITS_PER_V, rounded: the voltage a node moves in one step of dt/C = 200 V/A, in units of 2^-24 V.
pub const DTC_V_PER_A : u32 = 200;
pub const UNITS_PER_V : u32 = 16777216;
/// Corner indices for the accessors below.
pub const CORNER_TT : u32 = 0;
pub const CORNER_FF : u32 = 1;
pub const CORNER_SS : u32 = 2;
pub const CORNER_FS : u32 = 3;
pub const CORNER_SF : u32 = 4;
/// The held-out R2 points: point k = 1..N is Vgs (Vsg) = 1.5 frac(k R2_A1), Vds (Vsd) = 1.5 frac(k R2_A2).
pub const R2_A1 : f64 = 0.7548776662466927;
pub const R2_A2 : f64 = 0.5698402909980532;
/// The R2 points given per corner: 1000 for tt, 200 for the others.
pub const R2_TT_COUNT : u32 = 1000;
pub const R2_OTHER_COUNT : u32 = 200;
/// The charge tables: an entry is Q / C_REF in units of 2^-24 V, relative to the grid origin, plus Q_OFFSET (so no entry is negative).
pub const C_REF_FF : u32 = 500;
pub const Q_OFFSET : u32 = 2097152;
/// The capacitances ngspice itself reports at the NMOS operating point Vgs = 0.9 V, Vds = 0.75 V, in aF (deck psp103_q_tt.cir, block op_n):
/// the channel capacitances cdd, cdg, cgg and, each apart, the gate-source and gate-drain overlaps and the drain junction.
pub const OP_CDD_AF : u32 = 81;
pub const OP_CDG_AF : u32 = 1398;
pub const OP_CGG_AF : u32 = 3483;
pub const OP_CGSOL_AF : u32 = 641;
pub const OP_CGDOL_AF : u32 = 615;
pub const OP_CJD_AF : u32 = 328;

; --- order-sensitive folds of the pasted numbers (fold of linear.t27): a changed number changes a pin ---------
pub const PIN_TT : u64 = 0x814310C06BAD1CA9;
pub const PIN_FF : u64 = 0xE6FFE9D8D46CF1F9;
pub const PIN_SS : u64 = 0x1A69AE5C040FEA68;
pub const PIN_FS : u64 = 0x61CDCDFBFA1B2459;
pub const PIN_SF : u64 = 0x13F09713FAAE89F6;
pub const PIN_TT_HELD : u64 = 0x4D63964ABAF11967;
pub const PIN_OTHER_HELD : u64 = 0x63623E6E75519E74;
pub const PIN_TRAN : u64 = 0x859D61FDD24C4A10;
/// The charge tables of corners tt and ss, in the order qd_n, qg_n, qd_p, qg_p (the four tables of a corner folded one after another).
/// The 500 fF waveform INV500_BE.
pub const PIN_TRAN500 : u64 = 0xB35700152266D9B9;
pub const PIN_TT_Q : u64 = 0xFE5696611BC5AB3B;
pub const PIN_SS_Q : u64 = 0x06627578C483E909;

